==Trivia==
*The Arrows are 1 of 10 [[cards]] associated with archery, with the others being [[Archers]], [[Tower Princess]], [[X-Bow]], [[Princess]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Super Archers]], [[Archer Queen]], and the [[Little Prince]].
**The Arrows, Archers, and the Tower Princess are the only cards associated with archery that are unlocked in [[Training Camp]].
**In the Japanese and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Arrows' name translates to "Rain of Arrows".
**In the Chinese language setting of the game, it is revealed that the barrage consists of 10,000 arrows.
*The Arrows are 1 of 7 cards that are already unlocked for the player when they start playing the game, the others being [[Minions]], Archers, [[Knight]], Tower Princess, [[Giant]], and [[Fireball]]. Despite this, the game recognizes that those cards are unlocked in the Training Camp.
*The Arrows are one of the first [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] cards to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the [[Zap]], Fireball, and [[Rocket]].
*The Arrows are one of the first spells to be featured in a [[Loading Screens|Loading Screen]], alongside the Fireball and Rocket.
*The Arrows are one of the first spells to receive a card render, alongside the Rocket and [[Barbarian Barrel]].
*The Arrows' card render is identical to its card image.
*Although not available as a spell, the Arrows reappear as [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Archer Archer]'s active ability in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
** In Clash Royale, it is called "Arrows", but in Squad Busters, it is called "Arrow Volley".
*The Arrows are the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Arrows are the subject of a few [[Clans|Clan]] badges.
**The Arrows are the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].
*The Arrows were featured in the winning decks of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Arrows were featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VxEzjdKQ4HA Clash Royale Helsinki Tournament], by a player called Jason.
**The Arrows were featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/vRrgTfqRdpw?si=YDASUydL7qNm9QZz Clash Royale League 2023 Tournament], by a player called Mugi.
**The Arrows were featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/Sa0QOSJ5AVY?si=Hlcj6efCnFhxfDYe Clash Royale League 2024 Tournament], by a player called Mohamed Light.
*The initial balance change for Arrows on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/3/2025)|4/3/2025 Balance Update]] was a Crown Tower Damage decrease to 10% (from 25%), but it was changed to an Area Radius decrease [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-69-balance-wip-march-2025?lang=en last minute].
*Before the Arrows' card release, Arrows' Damage were increased by 9%.
